    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0471" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.51/196.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Hartman</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-06T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 6, 1915—2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s July 23, 5 p.m. Department waiting with interest reply of Foreign
                    Office regarding its attitude conditional flotation of loan.</p>
                <pb facs="0472" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/>
                <p>For your information Cooper telegraphs from London in part as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Have private information Government intends get Congress pass act
                            authorizing Executive suspend payments until differences with railway
                            company settled.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Can you confirm this?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
